+# Privacy-by-design notes
+
+## Third-party audit
+| Resource | Finding | Action |
+|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` hero image (CSS `background`) | Every visitor's IP, UA and page URL (Referer) was sent to a third party on load | Removed; hero uses a local CSS gradient. To restore a photo, self-host it under `/assets` (CSP `img-src 'self'` already permits it). |
+| Fonts, analytics, trackers, embeds | None present | CSP `default-src 'none'` keeps it that way |
+
+## Data minimization
+- No scripts, cookies, forms, storage or analytics on the page; CSP `script-src 'none'`, `connect-src 'none'`.
+- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` (header and meta) so URLs never leak.
+- Permissions-Policy disables sensor/device APIs and FLoC/Topics.
+
+## Secure handling
+- CSS moved to `styles.css` and inline `style` removed, so no `'unsafe-inline'` is needed.
+- `_headers` (Netlify/Cloudflare Pages format) sets CSP incl. `frame-ancestors`, HSTS, nosniff, COOP/CORP, X-Frame-Options.
+  The `statikk` dev server ignores it; port these to the real host if it differs.
+- Meta CSP is a fallback; `frame-ancestors` and HSTS only work as real headers.
+- Any future third-party resource or script must be justified here and added to the CSP explicitly.
